  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is trimethoprim, a small weakly basic 2,4-diaminopyrimidine with established clinical CNS penetration (CSF/plasma ~0.4). The closest transferable experimental analog, mescaline, shows measurable brain/serum exposure (~0.33) for the trimethoxyphenyl base motif. The high-scoring fail records come from larger, more efflux-prone, acidic, or permanently charged molecules that are mechanistically distinct from the query. Therefore, meaningful CNS access is predicted.",
